==Battleground==
*1 [[Chocolate Doge]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*4 [[Vlad de Sable]]s spawn after 1.33 seconds<sup>40f</sup>, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Glowstick Guys]] spawn after 0.67 seconds<sup>20f</sup>, delay 2~5 seconds<sup>60f~150f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Pumpkin Doge]]s spawn after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*30 [[Vlad de Sable]]s spawn after 1.33 seconds<sup>40f</sup>, delay 5~10 seconds<sup>150f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Bears Be Back]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Cat Kart P (Enemy)|Cat Kart P]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**7 [[Chocolate Doge]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
**3 [[Count Owlbrow]]s spawn, delay 26.67~40 seconds<sup>800f~1,200f</sup>.
**1 [[Bears Be Back]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is a nightmare without the right lineup. The Count Owlbrows will destroy your Erasers in one hit, Bears Be Back will crowd-control anything that lives into submission, and Cat Kart P requires the use of many meatshields, ideally [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] clones.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Cat]] - A useful meatshield that can dodge attacks from both Chocolate Doge and Bears Be Back, while serving as a cheap, disposable meatshield for Cat Kart P. Note that without his [[True Form]], he can't survive a Mini-Wave from Chocolate Doge in {{2c}} and {{3c}}.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Mohawk Cat]] - Similar to Brainwashed Cat, except it trades Dodge for total Wave Immunity, which is more useful against Chocolate Doge in higher Crowns. Also has a low cost and a great research Combo.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]] - Immune to the annoying status effects of Bears Be Back, and easily shrugs off hits from Count Owlbrow and Cat Kart P. Needs research combos, such as [[Mini-Saurus (Combo)|Mini-Saurus]], to function well.
*[[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] - Is Immune to Waves, and has good Long-Distance damage, letting it hit the backline using Chocolate Doge as a stepping stone. Also deals massive damage to Cat Kart P, which is very helpful for killing it quickly.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] - Has massive damage vs Chocolate Doge and Bears Be Back. Has no Wave Immunity, but also has the health to just tank the Waves. With his Wave Attack Talent, he can also hit every enemy on the field at once which is very worthwhile.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Squirtgun Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Aquablaster Saki]] - Snipes the Count Owlbrows and Bears Be Back for huge damage. She can't hit the Chocolate Doges, but this can be used to her advantage by stacking her on them. If you don't have her True Form, use her Normal Form instead, so that she can hit the Chocolate Doges as well, since they're already decently tanky.

